WEBVTT

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.290
Madame Vastra.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.490
Thank God.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.620
I bet you've never seen anything like this.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:39.510
Well...

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.180
Not since I was a little girl.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.130
It's huge, don't you think?

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.960
Dinosaurs were all about this size.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.960
And I think I know it's a female.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.880
They weren't all big. I saw fossils.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.140
And I was there.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.140
It's fascinating.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.990
But do you know what this dinosaur does in the tamiz?

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.700
She must have traveled through time.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:10.140
- Jenny? - Travel through time?

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.340
She's shaking.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.340
It seems like something is stuck in her throat.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.340
Excuse me, but how could she have traveled through time?

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:18.690
I don't know. Maybe because of something she ate.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.340
Step back! Step back!

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.230
Look! She just laid an egg.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:40.480
She just cracked a blue cabin with the word "Police" written on it.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.480
Your interpretation of animal biology worries me a little.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:46.700
Tardis?

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.120
It seems so.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.670
We're going to take care of everything, Inspector!

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.890
But if this thing starts to disperse?

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:56.400
Place these lanterns on the tracks and on the bridges.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.000
You will thus encircle the creature. Place them one at a time.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
"What are they for?"

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.400
They emit a signal that will repel the dinosaur and force it to stay in the circle.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:13.330
"Jenny! Strax! With me!"

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.330
"So it's him? It's the doctor?"

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:19.330
A giant dinosaur straight from the bottom of the ages who has just vomited a blue cabin.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.440
Who travels in space.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.500
"Don't make too active conclusions. Strax, you want to?"

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:41.270
Get out of this cabin and surrender to the splendor of the Sontarian Empire!

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:52.120
The dinosaurs are chasing me, but I think I sowed them.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:30.000
You two, you who are green and you who are not green, or maybe it's the other way around.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Let's not fall into prejudices.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:45.490
Oh, you remember my dear, the other, who is not me, the one who always asks questions.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.840
I have trouble with the names.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:49.730
Clara.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.750
It may be Clara or maybe not.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:52.840
It's the lottery.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.840
I'm telling you it's Clara.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:54.840
Yes, it's possible.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:55.840
Oh, you're going to close it at the end!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.220
Oh!

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.000
You!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.840
"Me too, you have a dinosaur!"

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.590
"A dinosaur, sorry."

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.710
"Doctor, listen to me, you have to stay calm, relax."

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.710
"And I'm not flirting with you, actually."

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:15.360
"There must have been a problem."

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.340
"A problem? What problem?"

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:21.470
"You're regenerated?"

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:30.000
"I remember you, cafeteria, you were a small, very small robot head."

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.360
And now, you've let yourself go.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:40.840
Frequency!

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.660
I beg your pardon?

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.360
Voluntary Sonic, shut up!

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.920
She gives him a headache.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:47.740
But to whom?

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:50.740
To my dear companion!

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.940
This is just a way of talking, don't you have any idea?

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:53.940
How do you know?

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.440
Finally, Clara, you know I'm talking about the dinosaur!

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.320
It's not him, Clara, it's me, Clara.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:07.040
You're exactly the same size. You should probably wear badges.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:15.280
Why? Why are you doing this to me? Why you? Why? Why are you all turning dark?

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.240
Satan, stop that.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.090
We're not turning dark.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:20.370
It doesn't matter.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.270
Come on everyone, come on! Let's take a break!

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.730
I don't understand. Who is it? Where is the doctor?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:39.960
He's there. It's him.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:44.200
The doctor.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:48.240
Well, in that case, let's go for a walk.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.820
I don't understand! I don't know what it is!

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.820
But who invented this room?

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:45.820
Doctor, please, you have to lie down and rest.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:48.820
It doesn't make sense, look, there's only one bed and nothing else in this room.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:51.130
Why is there only one bed and nothing else in this room?

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:54.130
Because this room is a bedroom, it's made to sleep.

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:58.280
Okay, and what do you do when you wake up?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.000
You look at the room.

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.430
So you have a piece that you don't use when you're awake?

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:08.070
But what's the point? You don't take advantage of it and you don't look in the mirror!

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.570
The image he's sending is furious!

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:13.650
I beg you! You have to lie down, you can't stop losing consciousness!

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:18.120
Of course I can't stop losing consciousness, with all these beds, and why so much attention to me?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.370
Tell me, why so much politeness?

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.510
It's simply because your well-being matters to him!

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:26.640
You too are polite, you are contaminated with each other, it's all so...

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:30.000
English! So polite that it becomes so wrong!

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.620
Doctor, I have a problem and I will need your help.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:37.040
Finally someone who asks me for help instead of bringing it to me.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.880
I have a hard time finding sleep.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.040
If that's the case, I won't do it in your place.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.080
I never go to bed, I take a nap.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.240
Oh really? That's interesting.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.780
And when do you take these naps?

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.780
When the person in front of me starts talking.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:54.080
I use his lines to listen to only mine and so I save time.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.460
Make me save time, doctor.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:00.000
Do you want to project a perfect image of sleep

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.000
in the very heart of my mind.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.000
You want to create a psychic connection with me?

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.000
Given the size of my brain, it would be as if I threw a piano at you.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.020
Go slowly then.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:11.480
I'll try.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:12.480
Get ready.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:16.690
Piano.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:19.440
I love monkeys, they're so funny.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.440
Oh, I see.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:22.440
Do you consider people like monkeys now?

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.320
No, my dear.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.790
People are primates.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.640
But men, I consider them like monkeys.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:30.900
So what do we do?

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.270
He needs rest.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.270
Okay, but how do we fix it?

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:34.270
Repair it?

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:38.660
How do we get it back?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:43.540
Jenny, I'm going to my little salon, would you mind bringing me my veil?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:46.570
Why do foreigners have to come and visit us?

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:50.480
It would seem that one of them is already among us.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:58.260
What did I do wrong?

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.310
The dinosaur doesn't seem to be doing very well.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.690
What's wrong with him?

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:05.760
I don't know.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:09.830
It's the doctor who's talking about the dinosaur.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:14.830
I'm sorry, madam, but she doesn't like to wait.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:20.380
Where does this face come from?

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.580
Why does he have wrinkles? He just recovered.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:27.430
And how come his hair is gray? He just got them.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:30.000
It's still him, madam. You saw him recover.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:32.810
I know, yes, I saw it.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:33.860
It's true.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.780
So?

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:35.640
It's just that...

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:36.910
That what?

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.700
Nothing.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:47.630
If... If Vastra changed, if she became different, if she no longer looked like the one you like...

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:58.480
Actually, I don't like her, madam. No, I love her. And speaking of differences, she's a lizard.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:29.090
I'm alone.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:35.280
The world that trembled under my feet.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:43.380
The trees and the sky have disappeared.

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:51.200
And I am alone now, all alone.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.570
Oh, you know what she says.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:56.070
The wind does not caress anymore, it dies.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.670
The world has become gray.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:06.200
But I am alone, yes, all alone.

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:14.970
They don't see me, they don't recognize me.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:18.010
What do you mean, they don't see her? Everyone can see her.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:23.290
No! Mrs. Vastra is waiting.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.490
Okay, I'll follow you.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:28.160
I'm going to take you to her right away.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:29.660
May I take your coat?

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.340
- I don't wear a coat. - What's all that then?

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:35.020
Clothes.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.940
- May I take your clothes? - No, thank you.

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.940
- Are you wearing a hat? - These are my hair.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:42.440
I think it's a hat, can you let me check?

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:55.620
- Oh, I'm sure of it. - Who's behind this then?

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:58.110
- The government. - The government?

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.000
Hey, it's another one of their twisted tricks.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:03.420
It's a dinosaur, Alf, with flesh and bones.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:05.020
They're capable of anything to lure us in.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.020
The nonsense you can tell, Alfie.

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.710
Well, don't come back too late, okay?

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:11.150
- You know me? - Yes.

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:12.380
Precisely.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:25.590
The shot, it's Lac, the Babelais.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.360
He's not very realistic.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:29.510
You have good eyes.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.400
Indeed, I have good eyes, very good eyes.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:33.940
My eyes are a real gift.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:36.630
In that case, I accept it.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.520
What then?

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.040
Your gift.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.560
I don't have very good eyes.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.760
And then?

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:48.360
Why are you wearing your sail?

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.940
And then?

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:53.660
And then, a huge dinosaur swallowed us.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.120
You probably noticed.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.110
How did it happen?

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:58.390
I don't know.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:00.000
I don't know, we were...

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:04.750
We were crushed, I don't know where and when. The TARDIS is broken and the doctor has disappeared.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.080
He didn't disappear, he's in his room.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:12.030
Okay, he changed.

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:15.430
He regenerated, he renewed his envelope.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:16.100
Okay.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:20.060
Why this cynical smile?

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:22.820
I don't smile.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:26.930
Externally, no. But I'm used to seeing through a veil.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:29.510
What amused you when I said that?

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.980
He was renewed, that's not true.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:35.860
He doesn't look renewed, he looks older.

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:37.980
You thought he was young?

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.100
He looked young.

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:42.790
This gentleman could have been your handsome and young friend.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:43.870
Your lover, maybe.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:45.210
What the fuck?

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:46.830
But he's the Doctor.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:50.290
He traveled the universe for I don't know how many centuries.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.850
He saw stars crumble to dust.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.410
So why not try flirting with a mountain chain?

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.290
I didn't try flirting with him.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:58.900
He tried flirting with you.

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:02.330
- What do you mean? - He looked young.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.410
Who do you think it was for?

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:08.950
Everyone.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.900
If I wear a veil and a face,

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:14.280
it's for the same reason.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:15.850
What reason?

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.850
The oldest reason to exist.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:20.040
To be accepted.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.410
Marie and I are married, and to preserve appearances, we make people believe that she is my domestic.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:11.230
That does not explain why it is I who must serve tea, even in private.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:12.720
Shut up, finally.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:14.880
She looks good, doesn't she?

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:20.820
If I wear a veil, it is to hide what many like to call my disfiguration.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:28.250
I do not wear it out of politeness or convenience, but to prove the value of the heart of people.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:31.250
You are judging me.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:36.570
The Doctor has regenerated in your presence.

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:39.120
The young man has disappeared, the veil has risen.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.810
He trusted you and you alone.

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:43.030
Do you judge him?

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:52.210
It's you.

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:14.980
You're boring, not my kind.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:22.920
My kind?

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:25.330
Corrêl, the Roman emperor,

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.340
last Antonin and the Austrian philosopher.

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:28.600
And an unequal bassist,

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:30.000
Dr. Adiné, when it comes to

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.000
It's the only poster I had when I was 15, the only one I've ever had.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.000
I'm not sure you know who you're talking to, Mrs. Vastra.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.000
I never had the slightest interest in the little miners.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:43.000
And for your information, if there is a person who could flirt with a mountain chain, she is in front of you.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:49.860
It is not because my pretty Minois makes you turn your head that you must believe me as superficial as that.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:58.270
Sorry.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:03.650
Well, it's not too early.

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:04.850
The earth is finally shaking.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:08.030
I often wondered what you looked like in anger.

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:10.730
Are you married?

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:15.590
The Doctor needs us and especially you.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:19.560
He is lost in the depths of his ruins and we have to show him the way out.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:25.060
When did you take off your veil?

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:28.800
When you stopped seeing him.

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:38.560
My beautiful and giant companion!

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:39.710
Hey!

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.320
Sorry!

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:44.320
Sorry, it's all my fault!

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:47.350
My time machine got stuck in your throat!

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:49.550
It happens, I brought you here by accident!

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.950
That's often how I make meetings, but don't worry, I promise you!

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.410
That I will bring you back home!

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:56.500
I promise you!

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:58.010
Whatever it takes!

00:17:58.460 --> 00:17:59.070
Me?

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.000
I promise!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:14.700
Dinosaur, his safety, I promise you to go home soon!

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:19.060
No, don't do that!

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:21.960
That noise, it was coming from the river.

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:23.460
The dinosaur...

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:27.590
Strax! Move the cage right now!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:46.310
Sorry, I will have to set you free from your animal of company

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.310
From my what?

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:48.870
The farm, I'm talking to the horse

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:56.470
What are you doing?

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:23.400
Don't differentiate them!

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:32.260
"What happened in your opinion?"

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:34.580
"I do not know, but I fear a diabolical act."

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.870
"We should have warned the doctor."

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:41.310
"He is not ready to leave the bed."

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:43.600
"Caution in the turns, it slips a little up there."

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:59.360
"More fast!"

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:00.000
"I really am."

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:10.910
The doctor!

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:16.530
Where there is a problem, you find the doctor.

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:21.660
She was right.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:27.380
I brought her here to see what they were doing.

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:29.380
Who or what could have done such a thing?

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:35.440
Are you asking for forgiveness?

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:39.860
No, that's not the point.

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:42.770
That's not where we need to start.

