You don't always say that.

00:36:58.350 --> 00:37:00.000
Look, don't look.

00:37:00.060 --> 00:37:09.450
- You told me to look! - Without looking.

00:37:09.450 --> 00:37:16.710
- I don't see anything weird, he's eating. - Really?

00:37:30.280 --> 00:37:31.060
They don't eat.

00:37:31.060 --> 00:37:33.430
There's something else they don't do.

00:37:55.280 --> 00:37:57.040
- We're different. - Soon.

00:38:00.060 --> 00:38:02.510
How long have you been in apnea?

00:38:03.580 --> 00:38:06.400
We could just go back as if we had changed your life.

00:38:07.080 --> 00:38:09.190
- It happens very often. - Oh yes, of course.

00:38:34.540 --> 00:38:35.120
We're going to...

00:38:35.120 --> 00:38:46.230
...reject an eye to the card.

00:38:46.230 --> 00:38:48.300
What are they?

00:38:48.300 --> 00:38:49.120
No idea.

00:38:49.120 --> 00:38:51.200
But that's not the question, Clara.

00:38:51.200 --> 00:38:52.600
The question is:

00:38:52.600 --> 00:38:54.130
What is this restaurant?

00:38:54.130 --> 00:38:55.630
Okay, what is this restaurant?

00:38:55.630 --> 00:38:56.340
No idea.

00:39:07.960 --> 00:39:12.290
No worries. And I notice that there are no pictures.

00:39:12.290 --> 00:39:14.120
Would you have a children's menu?

00:39:14.120 --> 00:39:18.440
Do you have a home specialty?

00:39:18.440 --> 00:39:19.970
Yes, the cold.

00:39:19.970 --> 00:39:21.860
I don't like cold.

00:39:21.860 --> 00:39:26.680
And the rat, the brain trunk, the eyes.

00:39:26.680 --> 00:39:29.430
Are these often asked questions?

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.920
I do not believe that all this is on the map.

00:39:31.920 --> 00:39:35.280
In fact, it's us, the menu.

00:39:35.280 --> 00:39:36.880
Poumant.

00:39:36.880 --> 00:39:40.010
Pau.

00:39:40.010 --> 00:39:41.190
Excuse me.

00:39:46.700 --> 00:39:47.760
To hide.

00:39:47.760 --> 00:39:48.850
It's a face.

00:39:48.850 --> 00:39:51.850
Faye.

00:39:51.850 --> 00:39:54.480
No, it's a face.

00:39:56.120 --> 00:39:57.300
Yes.

00:39:57.300 --> 00:39:58.450
Yes, what?

00:39:58.450 --> 00:40:00.000
Yes, we have a menu.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:02.400
I'm naked for a child.

00:40:06.310 --> 00:40:08.280
We must recognize their effectiveness!

00:40:08.280 --> 00:40:10.930
Would you kill me if I don't get ecstatic?

00:40:23.030 --> 00:40:28.160
Hey, you're the boss. I demand to speak to the boss.

00:40:30.190 --> 00:40:32.810
This is not a real restaurant, is it?

00:40:32.810 --> 00:40:39.390
Yes, it's more like a kind of automated organ collection center for naive customers.

00:40:39.390 --> 00:40:40.710
Swinny tot without the turds.

00:40:40.710 --> 00:40:42.060
Where exactly are we?

00:40:42.060 --> 00:40:45.860
In fact, in an old space ship that has been buried for centuries.

00:40:45.860 --> 00:40:49.300
Functionally, in a dining room.

00:40:49.300 --> 00:40:51.320
Why is no one coming to get us then?

00:40:51.320 --> 00:40:52.360
We are alive.

00:40:52.360 --> 00:40:54.040
We are alive in a dining room?

00:40:54.040 --> 00:40:57.150
Precisely. It's cheaper than freezing us.

00:40:57.150 --> 00:40:58.760
Okay.

00:40:58.760 --> 00:40:59.670
Are you ready?

00:41:00.600 --> 00:41:03.430
- Yes, go ahead. - Don't let him roll.

00:41:03.520 --> 00:41:05.600
- No. - We only have one try.

00:41:05.680 --> 00:41:07.590
Next time, make a screwdriver that doesn't roll.

00:41:08.390 --> 00:41:15.360
- Let's go. - I...

00:41:17.270 --> 00:41:19.510
- It's in these moments that I miss Emy. - Who?

00:41:19.720 --> 00:41:23.750
- No, nothing. - Are you ready?

00:41:32.490 --> 00:41:34.710
Sorry, did I touch... something?

00:41:34.710 --> 00:41:39.140
No, the symbolism.

00:41:39.140 --> 00:41:45.240
You should make him add a vocal control.

00:41:45.240 --> 00:41:47.480
Genre, he already has it, doesn't he?

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:04.910
I don't know, I hope so.

00:42:04.910 --> 00:42:08.450
Are they the ones who killed the dinosaur?

00:42:08.450 --> 00:42:13.250
Well, if they really collect organs, a dinosaur is a real gold mine.

00:42:13.250 --> 00:42:17.010
Why would robots steal organs? They are space traffickers.

00:42:17.010 --> 00:42:19.900
It's a good theory.

00:42:19.900 --> 00:42:23.700
Robots collecting spare parts.

00:42:23.700 --> 00:42:25.000
In fact, it speaks to me.

00:42:33.230 --> 00:42:37.550
Captain, my captain.

00:42:37.550 --> 00:42:38.610
He sees us?

00:42:38.610 --> 00:42:39.640
In sleep.

00:42:39.640 --> 00:42:40.410
You hope so?

00:42:40.410 --> 00:42:40.910
Yes.

00:42:40.910 --> 00:42:46.090
Oh, look!

00:42:46.090 --> 00:42:48.760
Ignore that we are here.

00:42:48.760 --> 00:42:51.600
Sure, not sure, one or the other.

00:42:51.600 --> 00:42:54.080
Okay, so he's half man, half robot.

00:42:54.080 --> 00:42:55.190
It's a cyborg, right?

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.190
Ooooooh...

00:43:01.190 --> 00:43:02.850
Look at these hands.

00:43:02.850 --> 00:43:04.100
Yes, what are these hands?

00:43:04.100 --> 00:43:04.760
Look at these hands.

00:43:04.760 --> 00:43:05.440
I'm looking.

00:43:05.440 --> 00:43:18.220
These hands don't come from the same body.

00:43:18.220 --> 00:43:21.410
I don't understand.

00:43:21.410 --> 00:43:23.270
I can't help you.

00:43:23.270 --> 00:43:25.940
See that?

00:43:25.940 --> 00:43:28.810
It's not a ordinary cyborg.

00:43:28.810 --> 00:43:30.000
And it's not a human that transforms.

00:43:32.560 --> 00:43:37.080
or who turns into humans, piece by piece.

00:43:37.080 --> 00:43:38.860
Is that what the restaurant is for?

00:43:38.860 --> 00:43:41.890
It must renew its stock continuously.

00:43:41.890 --> 00:43:44.940
We can taint the skin, but the organs, they rot.

00:43:44.940 --> 00:43:46.840
Some pieces seem from Roman times.

00:43:46.840 --> 00:43:54.040
I've been wondering since when it exists and if it really remains the original.

00:43:54.040 --> 00:43:56.660
On the other hand, the eyes seem to be recent.

00:44:35.980 --> 00:44:37.980
The brain that is still in reboot mode!

00:44:37.980 --> 00:44:38.860
Come on!

00:44:38.860 --> 00:44:41.780
I've seen this before!

00:44:41.780 --> 00:44:42.420
At your place!

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:00.450
I'm dead.

00:48:10.520 --> 00:48:11.620
Bring her to me.

00:48:33.680 --> 00:48:34.980
It's her first day.

00:48:38.500 --> 00:48:42.500
If you don't stop, I'll send you back from this school to the last one!

00:48:43.610 --> 00:48:44.410
Go ahead.

00:48:45.010 --> 00:48:46.110
You're lying.

00:48:56.210 --> 00:48:59.510
Where's the other one?

00:49:06.880 --> 00:49:09.100
There was another one. Where is he?

00:49:09.100 --> 00:49:10.530
Where is the other one?

00:49:10.530 --> 00:49:14.910
You will talk.

00:49:14.910 --> 00:49:18.400
You will be destroyed.

00:49:18.400 --> 00:49:23.490
You will talk.

00:49:23.490 --> 00:49:26.010
Yes, I know.

00:49:26.010 --> 00:49:27.410
Otherwise what?

00:49:27.410 --> 00:49:28.410
You will die.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:32.330
Go on, do it.

00:49:32.330 --> 00:49:49.470
Go on, do it.

00:49:49.470 --> 00:49:52.270
I won't answer your questions.

00:49:52.270 --> 00:49:55.340
So you have to do it. You have to kill me.

00:49:55.340 --> 00:49:58.770
Threats are useless without going through the act.

00:50:02.650 --> 00:50:04.350
You will tell us where the other one is.

00:50:04.350 --> 00:50:04.850
No!

00:50:05.970 --> 00:50:06.870
You will be destroyed.

00:50:06.870 --> 00:50:07.970
Destroy me then.

00:50:08.410 --> 00:50:09.610
And if you don't do it...

00:50:10.280 --> 00:50:12.480
Well, I won't believe a single one of your threats.

00:50:14.490 --> 00:50:15.690
Obviously, if I'm dead...

00:50:17.480 --> 00:50:18.980
I won't be able to tell you where the other one is.

00:50:20.900 --> 00:50:23.000
You have to keep this place a secret, don't you?

00:50:25.020 --> 00:50:26.820
Never start with the ultimate sanction.

00:50:27.390 --> 00:50:29.250
You have no choice but to step back.

00:50:33.900 --> 00:50:35.460
Humans feel the pain.

00:50:35.460 --> 00:50:40.500
Ah, threats are less risky, as I said, step back.

00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:45.540
The information can be obtained through your suffering.

00:50:45.540 --> 00:50:50.240
You're trying to scare me, because I'm already terribly afraid of dying.

00:50:50.240 --> 00:50:56.950
I will endure a lot of suffering for a very long time before letting go of the information that keeps me alive, you have time, you!

00:51:06.650 --> 00:51:11.430
What you can offer me is life, but you can't make threats to me, you can just negotiate.

00:51:11.430 --> 00:51:20.960
Because I'm... I'm really scared of you.

00:51:20.960 --> 00:51:25.800
And if you really know human feelings, you know that means you're in hell.

00:51:25.800 --> 00:51:29.760
We will not negotiate.

00:51:30.160 --> 00:51:32.020
You don't have a choice.

00:51:32.020 --> 00:51:35.690
I'll answer your questions if you answer mine.

00:51:35.690 --> 00:51:38.450
We won't answer your questions.

00:51:38.450 --> 00:51:39.810
Everyone turn around, I'm starting.

00:51:39.810 --> 00:51:41.390
Why did you kill the dinosaur?

00:51:41.390 --> 00:51:42.890
We won't answer your questions.

00:51:42.890 --> 00:51:43.790
Why did you kill the dinosaur?

00:51:43.790 --> 00:51:45.890
We won't answer your questions.

00:51:45.890 --> 00:51:48.920
Then you can kill me right away because I won't answer the first one.

00:52:00.510 --> 00:52:05.510
In the optical nerve of the dinosaur, there is a very useful component for our computer system.

00:52:05.510 --> 00:52:08.460
You burned a dinosaur for a spare part?

00:52:08.460 --> 00:52:11.250
No.

00:52:11.250 --> 00:52:17.310
You know what's in the optical nerve of a dinosaur, that means you've already seen it.

00:52:17.310 --> 00:52:20.020
And the other?

00:52:20.020 --> 00:52:22.880
How long have you been recycling?

00:52:22.880 --> 00:52:26.340
Given your state, there is not much left of it, what is the point?

00:52:31.240 --> 00:52:33.240
We will reach the promised land.

00:52:33.240 --> 00:52:37.970
The promised land, what is that?

00:52:37.970 --> 00:52:40.560
Where is the other?

00:52:40.560 --> 00:52:45.140
I don't know.

00:52:45.140 --> 00:52:49.910
But I know where he will be.

00:52:49.910 --> 00:52:52.390
Where he will be forever.

00:52:52.390 --> 00:52:57.110
The Doctor is always the Doctor.

00:53:00.350 --> 00:53:10.350
He will assure my Arian that I'm right.

00:53:10.350 --> 00:53:21.350
Hello, hello.

00:53:21.350 --> 00:53:24.100
Vile robot straight out of time.

00:53:24.100 --> 00:53:26.490
Thank you for all this free information.

00:53:26.490 --> 00:53:30.000
A meter fifty-five in size, you had no chance.

00:53:30.540 --> 00:53:31.440
Stop that.

00:53:34.980 --> 00:53:37.000
It's your source of energy.

00:53:37.000 --> 00:53:42.000
As weak as it is, I will use it to make everything jump if I see one thing that displeases me.

00:53:42.000 --> 00:53:45.000
Including karaoke and memes. So don't take any risks.

00:53:45.000 --> 00:53:48.500
You see, Clara, this is how we dress up, android.

00:53:48.500 --> 00:53:51.500
Yes, but I didn't have time to do it because I was abandoned.

00:53:51.500 --> 00:53:53.000
Sorry, well, not really.

00:53:53.000 --> 00:53:56.000
Adrenaline, you're doing pretty well. You had no chance, sir.

00:53:56.000 --> 00:53:58.000
Never try to manipulate a dictator.

00:53:58.000 --> 00:53:59.000
I'm not a dictator!

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:00.800
Yes, ma'am.

00:54:02.480 --> 00:54:03.680
Why are you here?

00:54:03.780 --> 00:54:05.370
Why did you invite us?

00:54:06.770 --> 00:54:08.870
The message? In the paper?

00:54:10.270 --> 00:54:11.270
It was you, wasn't it?

00:54:17.270 --> 00:54:22.410
I hate to see you in public. Please forget what just happened.

00:54:22.610 --> 00:54:23.610
Clara, say the word.

00:54:23.810 --> 00:54:25.610
- What word? - We didn't send you here without an emergency code.

00:54:25.810 --> 00:54:27.970
- I don't want to say it. - I already guessed it.

00:54:28.450 --> 00:54:29.570
- I don't want to say it. - Jeronimo.

00:54:41.100 --> 00:54:44.100
Don't move and drop your weapons in the name of the Britannian Empire!

00:54:45.010 --> 00:54:48.500
Sorry.

00:54:48.500 --> 00:54:49.830
I won't stop telling you.

00:54:49.830 --> 00:54:51.220
Take the stairs.

00:54:51.220 --> 00:54:52.720
Oh, look, the cavalry.

00:54:52.720 --> 00:54:56.220
I burned a beautiful creature for a few centimeters of optical nerve.

00:54:56.220 --> 00:54:58.650
What do you think you can accomplish, little man?

00:54:58.650 --> 00:55:00.000
Separate yourself, Fashtra.

00:55:01.600 --> 00:55:06.300
The building above has been cleaned in every corner by our care.

00:55:06.300 --> 00:55:07.660
The authorities have been warned.

00:55:07.660 --> 00:55:08.900
Did you call the police?

00:55:08.900 --> 00:55:10.690
We'll never do it, André Timmer!

00:55:10.690 --> 00:55:11.680
You see?

00:55:11.680 --> 00:55:15.910
Destroy us if you want. They will close your restaurant anyway.

00:55:15.910 --> 00:55:18.040
That should sound better than that.

00:55:18.040 --> 00:55:18.950
So?

00:55:18.950 --> 00:55:20.230
We will destroy you.

00:55:30.570 --> 00:55:32.400
No, you won't do anything.

00:55:32.400 --> 00:55:35.050
You are magic, you control yourself.

00:55:35.050 --> 00:55:37.050
You kill to survive.

00:55:37.050 --> 00:55:38.050
You're not a murderer.

00:55:38.050 --> 00:55:40.050
He's not what? We're in a slaughterhouse.

00:55:40.050 --> 00:55:42.050
What's the difference between this restaurant and the others?

00:55:42.050 --> 00:55:44.050
You're not vegetarian, if I'm not mistaken.

00:55:44.050 --> 00:55:46.050
It's over. Killing us won't change anything.

00:55:46.050 --> 00:55:47.050
What's the point?

00:55:47.050 --> 00:55:48.050
Find the promised land.

00:55:48.050 --> 00:55:50.050
You've been living here for millions of years.

00:55:50.050 --> 00:55:51.050
It's time you know it doesn't exist.

00:55:51.050 --> 00:55:53.050
I'm looking for paradise.

00:55:53.050 --> 00:55:54.050
Yes, that's good.

00:55:54.050 --> 00:55:56.050
And me too, but I won't make it either.

00:55:57.980 --> 00:55:59.450
Doctor!

00:55:59.450 --> 00:56:00.000
I'm going with you.

00:56:00.060 --> 00:56:02.500
With the rescue capsule, destroy what it must be.

00:56:02.500 --> 00:56:04.160
The rescue capsule?

00:56:04.160 --> 00:56:07.480
This ship is old, several million years old, its capsule will not fly!

00:56:07.480 --> 00:56:08.800
It has been repaired.

00:56:08.800 --> 00:56:10.430
With what?

00:56:10.430 --> 00:56:11.670
With you.

00:56:11.670 --> 00:56:14.880
In defensive position, everyone!

00:56:14.880 --> 00:56:18.040
Doctor, he's on target!

00:56:18.040 --> 00:56:19.900
Your friend is smart.

00:56:19.900 --> 00:56:21.830
He knows you shouldn't follow me.

00:56:32.880 --> 00:56:36.130
Here we are, we have arrived, it's here. Come with me.

00:56:36.130 --> 00:56:44.400
Our intention is to leave. If yours is to prevent us, well, in that case, we will get down to business.

00:56:44.400 --> 00:56:52.080
Lord, what is it that has brought us here this time?

00:56:54.740 --> 00:56:59.480
The restaurant is closed.

00:57:07.610 --> 00:57:08.970
Don't let anyone in!

00:57:08.970 --> 00:57:10.240
No one!

00:57:10.240 --> 00:57:11.240
Understood?

00:57:11.240 --> 00:57:23.020
What are you doing here?

00:57:23.020 --> 00:57:25.280
I have the horrible feeling that I will have to kill you.

00:57:25.280 --> 00:57:29.160
I thought you would appreciate a drink before.

00:57:30.220 --> 00:57:39.540
In any case, I do.

00:57:39.540 --> 00:57:53.750
51st century, is that it?

00:57:53.750 --> 00:57:55.160
A temporary ship.

00:57:55.160 --> 00:57:56.810
Blocked in the past.

00:57:56.810 --> 00:57:59.540
You try to get home, but by making detours.

00:58:00.320 --> 00:58:03.720
- I'm looking for the promised land. - Yes, you don't stop saying it.

00:58:03.720 --> 00:58:14.500
Okay, your restaurant is made with parts of your old ship, but you're wasting your time. It will never fly.

00:58:14.500 --> 00:58:17.560
- The rescue module is viable. - How can it be?

00:58:17.560 --> 00:58:23.430
It is impossible to repair a ship from human remains. This story really reminds me of something.

00:58:23.430 --> 00:58:29.540
Okay, that's very clever.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:31.350
And the source of energy?

00:58:31.350 --> 00:58:42.940
The skin.

00:58:42.940 --> 00:58:45.520
Go back to the station.

00:58:45.520 --> 00:58:47.910
We're going to need reinforcements.

00:58:47.910 --> 00:58:50.270
What do I tell them?

00:58:50.270 --> 00:58:51.540
Attention!

00:58:51.540 --> 00:58:54.360
Get ready, my dear!

00:58:54.360 --> 00:58:55.880
The larger the camp,

00:58:55.880 --> 00:58:57.890
the twenty, the thirty!

00:58:57.890 --> 00:59:00.000
Those up there were only their own!

00:59:00.090 --> 00:59:01.730
These guys know how to fight!

00:59:01.730 --> 00:59:03.530
I'm waiting for them to resist us!

00:59:05.250 --> 00:59:07.850
Don't be afraid, boy! We'll get them with our own hands!

00:59:20.420 --> 00:59:23.680
The S.S. Marie Antoinette.

00:59:23.680 --> 00:59:25.680
Totally out of control robots.

00:59:25.680 --> 00:59:27.320
Depressing human beings.

00:59:27.320 --> 00:59:29.920
It's really familiar to me, but I...

00:59:30.030 --> 00:59:31.440
I can't remember.

00:59:31.440 --> 00:59:32.860
How would you kill me?

00:59:32.860 --> 00:59:37.230
"Major ship of Madame de Pompadour."

00:59:37.230 --> 00:59:40.510
No, I don't remember.

00:59:40.510 --> 00:59:43.200
How would you kill me?

00:59:43.200 --> 00:59:46.210
Take a glass first. It's human.

00:59:46.210 --> 00:59:48.530
I'm not human.

00:59:48.530 --> 00:59:49.910
Me neither.

00:59:49.910 --> 00:59:53.060
I'm dead, you bastard!

00:59:53.060 --> 00:59:54.920
*laughs*

00:59:54.920 --> 00:59:57.060
*coughs*

00:59:57.060 --> 01:00:00.000
*coughs*

01:00:07.550 --> 01:00:14.360
- Did you see it? - I saw anything.

01:00:14.360 --> 01:00:17.300
No, I don't believe it. Just one second.

01:00:17.300 --> 01:00:19.300
Droids and lies. I could write a book about it.

01:00:19.300 --> 01:00:23.080
The problem is that you're not really a droid anymore.

01:00:23.080 --> 01:00:26.120
You're more human than a machine.

01:00:26.120 --> 01:00:30.000
So tell me.

01:00:32.520 --> 01:00:40.140
How do you find the view?

01:00:40.140 --> 01:00:47.310
Magnificent.

01:00:47.310 --> 01:00:49.790
That's wrong!

01:00:49.790 --> 01:00:51.860
We are far from everything. Everything is smaller.

01:00:51.860 --> 01:00:53.760
I prefer to be down there.

01:00:53.760 --> 01:00:56.090
Everything is huge.

01:00:56.090 --> 01:00:58.410
Down there, everything is so important.

01:00:58.410 --> 01:01:00.000
Every detail, every moment.

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:02.660
every moment of life that clings to it.

01:01:02.660 --> 01:01:04.850
How could you kill me?

01:01:04.850 --> 01:01:08.910
The very fact of asking me this question proves that you no longer hold on to this existence.

01:01:08.910 --> 01:01:14.300
What will happen to the other droids when you die?

01:01:14.300 --> 01:01:17.630
You are the one controlling them, I suppose they will deactivate themselves.

01:01:17.630 --> 01:01:20.020
I will not die.

01:01:20.020 --> 01:01:21.450
I will reach the Promised Land.

01:01:21.450 --> 01:01:25.670
That doesn't exist, the Promised Land, it's just a superstition!

01:01:25.670 --> 01:01:30.000
Recovered from all the humanity that you have accumulated in this body for all these centuries.

01:01:30.030 --> 01:01:39.810
I'm not dead you are a ballet question and if you take a ballet and replace

01:01:39.810 --> 01:01:45.450
the sleeve and a little later the brush a gesture that you would do again

01:01:45.450 --> 01:01:49.510
again and again would always be the same ballet answer no of course not

01:01:49.510 --> 01:01:52.900
but you could always sweep the floor but finally it's unimportant

01:01:52.900 --> 01:01:56.620
forget what I just said you have replaced all your mechanical parts

01:01:56.620 --> 01:02:00.000
and organic and that constantly and permanently there is nothing left

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:02.680
of your original pieces, isn't it?

01:02:02.680 --> 01:02:05.890
You must have forgotten where this face came from.

01:02:05.890 --> 01:02:16.280
It can't end like this.

01:02:16.280 --> 01:02:18.370
But it must.

01:02:18.370 --> 01:02:20.970
And you know it, it's the only way out.

01:02:20.970 --> 01:02:23.730
Autodestruction goes against my basic programming.

01:02:23.730 --> 01:02:27.330
Death goes against mine.

01:02:39.980 --> 01:02:43.480
Stop breathing! They're stupid! Stop breathing!

01:03:01.980 --> 01:03:04.160
I won't make it, I won't make it.

01:03:04.160 --> 01:03:10.690
Take it easy my love, I can store oxygen in my lungs, we will share it.

01:03:10.690 --> 01:03:25.550
You are stronger than it seems, I hope you are too.

01:03:25.550 --> 01:03:30.000
But, can you finally admit that it's over?

01:03:31.400 --> 01:03:33.400
Do you have the guts to kill me?

01:03:33.400 --> 01:03:38.070
Those people down there, they have nothing but small arms.

01:03:38.070 --> 01:03:42.440
Don't underestimate me, I'm able to go far to protect them.

01:03:42.440 --> 01:03:44.140
Besides, I've already gone far to do it.

01:03:44.140 --> 01:03:48.090
And unlike you, I don't hope to reach the promised land.

01:03:48.090 --> 01:04:00.000
Read, of course, that one of us is lying about his basic programming.

01:04:02.880 --> 01:04:03.650
Yes.

01:04:03.650 --> 01:04:06.280
And we both know who it is.

01:05:12.030 --> 01:05:13.390
Are you sure he will come back here?

01:05:13.910 --> 01:05:15.910
There is no trace of him in the debris.

01:05:16.430 --> 01:05:19.070
Neither apart from Liamant Hill, where do you want him to go?

01:05:24.510 --> 01:05:25.990
I'm afraid we missed him.

01:05:37.040 --> 01:05:38.040
Come in, please.

01:05:38.040 --> 01:05:42.580
I hope I don't disturb you.

01:05:42.580 --> 01:05:45.850
Your company makes me happy. What can I do for you?

01:05:45.850 --> 01:05:47.850
That's exactly what I was going to ask of you.

01:05:47.850 --> 01:05:50.120
Obviously, I'm stuck here.

01:05:50.120 --> 01:05:52.920
A free room?

01:05:52.920 --> 01:05:56.510
You would be more than welcome in our home.

01:05:56.510 --> 01:06:00.000
But I've learned to...

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:03.600
A sure source that the Doctor will be back very soon for you.

01:06:03.600 --> 01:06:04.520
What source?

01:06:04.520 --> 01:06:09.510
The person who knows him better than anyone in the universe.

01:06:09.510 --> 01:06:10.500
Yes, who is that?

01:06:10.500 --> 01:06:16.220
Miss Clara Oswald.

01:06:16.220 --> 01:06:20.220
Who instinctively got dressed to go and see him.

01:06:20.220 --> 01:06:22.120
I just wanted to change.

01:06:22.120 --> 01:06:29.000
I'm not sure I know the Doctor anymore.

01:06:34.540 --> 01:06:36.940
It seems that you are wrong about that.

01:06:36.940 --> 01:06:40.320
Clara!

01:06:40.320 --> 01:06:42.630
Bend over, he needs it.

01:06:43.610 --> 01:06:44.500
Yes.

01:07:03.390 --> 01:07:05.470
- Have you redone the decoration? - Yes.

01:07:05.470 --> 01:07:08.740
- I don't like it. - I'm not convinced myself.

01:07:08.740 --> 01:07:10.740
There should be more round things on the wall.

01:07:10.740 --> 01:07:12.740
I had a lot of them before.

01:07:12.740 --> 01:07:27.970
I wonder where I put them.

01:07:27.970 --> 01:07:30.000
I'm a doctor. I've lived more than one life.

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:35.410
It's been more than 2000 years, and there's been nothing good.

01:07:35.410 --> 01:07:42.160
I've made a lot of mistakes, and it's high time to fix them.

01:07:42.160 --> 01:07:48.190
I'm not your little friend, Clara.

01:07:48.190 --> 01:07:49.720
I never thought of that.

01:07:49.720 --> 01:07:54.820
I didn't say it came from you.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:13.250
- What do you think? - Who put the ad in the paper?

01:08:13.250 --> 01:08:14.680
Who gave you my number?

01:08:14.680 --> 01:08:18.520
Remember, we gave you the number of a computer hotline

01:08:18.520 --> 01:08:21.120
and you ended up calling the TARDIS who gave you the number.

01:08:21.120 --> 01:08:22.810
The woman, the woman from the store.

01:08:22.810 --> 01:08:25.890
So there's a woman out there who keeps us together.

01:08:32.330 --> 01:08:37.650
- What do you think, Clara? - I'm at home.

01:08:37.650 --> 01:08:46.580
- If that's what you want. - I'm sorry.

01:08:46.580 --> 01:08:54.710
I'm sincerely sorry, but I don't recognize you anymore.

01:09:03.520 --> 01:09:05.530
Maybe he's your little friend.

01:09:05.530 --> 01:09:09.700
The farm. I don't have a little friend.

01:09:30.700 --> 01:09:35.210
The Doctor.

01:09:35.210 --> 01:09:39.880
What do you mean, "The Doctor"?

01:09:39.880 --> 01:09:43.070
I've been calling you since Trenzalor.

01:09:43.070 --> 01:09:43.990
I...

01:09:43.990 --> 01:09:46.170
Before I regenerate.

01:09:46.170 --> 01:09:48.850
It's coming, but it's getting closer.

01:09:49.930 --> 01:09:51.510
Oh yes, at full speed.

01:10:01.050 --> 01:10:11.320
I can feel it.

01:10:11.320 --> 01:10:14.280
Why are you doing this?

01:10:14.280 --> 01:10:18.590
I think it's going to be a huge thing.

01:10:18.590 --> 01:10:21.680
And I know you must be scared.

01:10:21.680 --> 01:10:26.020
And whatever the degree of your fear, Clara, the man who is with you right now...

01:10:26.020 --> 01:10:29.060
I hope so.

01:10:30.280 --> 01:10:32.400
Believe me, he's way more scared than you.

01:10:32.400 --> 01:10:35.730
Way more scared than you can imagine.

01:10:35.730 --> 01:10:40.190
He needs you.

01:10:40.190 --> 01:10:43.760
So, who is it?

01:10:43.760 --> 01:10:45.190
It's the Doctor.

01:10:45.190 --> 01:10:47.000
It's the Doctor?

01:10:47.000 --> 01:10:49.270
Yes.

01:10:49.270 --> 01:10:51.770
Your old man.

01:10:51.770 --> 01:10:55.220
Hey, tell me I'm not old, soft or old?

01:11:00.830 --> 01:11:04.450
- He has grey hair? - Yes.

01:11:04.450 --> 01:11:09.860
I beg you, Clara, do it for me.

01:11:09.860 --> 01:11:12.130
Help him, please.

01:11:12.130 --> 01:11:17.220
Go on, don't be afraid.

01:11:30.480 --> 01:11:32.130
Clara.

01:11:32.130 --> 01:11:45.810
I missed you.

01:11:45.810 --> 01:11:53.760
So what?

01:11:53.760 --> 01:11:55.510
I asked you a question.

01:11:55.510 --> 01:11:58.450
Are you going to help me?

01:11:58.450 --> 01:11:59.800
You listened to us.

01:12:01.690 --> 01:12:06.050
I didn't need to listen to you, I was the one calling.

01:12:06.050 --> 01:12:15.610
So you don't see me, you look at me, but without seeing me.

01:12:15.610 --> 01:12:17.840
Realize what it does.

01:12:17.840 --> 01:12:24.940
I'm not on the phone, I'm here.

01:12:24.940 --> 01:12:27.170
Here, in front of you.

01:12:30.570 --> 01:12:35.640
I beg you, Cid, to see me.

01:13:01.440 --> 01:13:02.440
Thank you for what?

01:13:02.440 --> 01:13:07.390
For calling me.

01:13:08.600 --> 01:13:14.600
Sorry Clara, I think I'm no longer a very tactful person.

01:13:14.600 --> 01:13:18.680
I'm not sure you have a choice.

01:13:18.680 --> 01:13:19.680
As you wish.

01:13:19.680 --> 01:13:22.710
In fact, I'm not at home here.

01:13:22.710 --> 01:13:26.520
Sorry, I must have missed something on the way.

01:13:26.520 --> 01:13:28.880
Where are we?

01:13:28.880 --> 01:13:30.000
Glasgow.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:31.000
I think so, yes, yes.

01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:33.080
Ah! Perfect for you.

01:13:33.080 --> 01:13:34.580
Scottish, no?

01:13:35.640 --> 01:13:38.520
Yes. Well, what if we...

01:13:38.520 --> 01:13:42.240
We were going to have a coffee or...

01:13:42.240 --> 01:13:43.890
French fries.

01:13:43.890 --> 01:13:47.620
Or something else. French fries and a coffee.

01:13:47.620 --> 01:13:48.700
A coffee.

01:13:48.700 --> 01:13:49.700
A coffee is perfect.

01:13:49.700 --> 01:13:50.640
You invite me.

01:13:50.640 --> 01:13:52.010
But I don't have any money.

01:13:52.010 --> 01:13:55.510
Go to Quémander.

01:13:55.510 --> 01:13:57.510
Quémander is not my kind either.

01:13:57.510 --> 01:14:00.000
No. But for that either, you don't have the choice.

01:14:20.960 --> 01:14:23.940
I am Missy, here you are.

01:14:23.940 --> 01:14:27.010
I hope my little friend wasn't too mean.

01:14:30.380 --> 01:14:33.300
-Tamy? -Did he push you out of this thing?

01:14:33.300 --> 01:14:36.240
Where did you fall? I didn't see well.

01:14:36.790 --> 01:14:44.280
He can be very mean sometimes, except with me of course, because he loves me so much.

01:14:44.280 --> 01:14:49.570
As for me, I like his new face. I might keep it.

01:14:49.570 --> 01:14:55.920
-Where am I? -Where do you think you are?

01:14:55.920 --> 01:14:59.920
Look around you. You have succeeded.

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:01.960
"La Terre Promise"

01:15:01.960 --> 01:15:04.840
"Bienvenue au Jardin des Taines"

01:15:06.850 --> 01:15:11.210
"Au Paradis"

01:15:15.780 --> 01:15:28.730
"Where the hell have you been?"

01:15:28.730 --> 01:15:29.660
"It's not my fault, I got to..."

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:31.240
By what?

01:15:31.650 --> 01:15:33.110
You can always find something. Come on.

01:15:33.840 --> 01:15:34.200
Where are we going?

01:15:34.900 --> 01:15:35.820
Into darkness.

01:15:36.760 --> 01:15:38.860
Welcome to the most dangerous place in the universe.

01:15:43.820 --> 01:15:44.160
They're coming.

01:15:44.590 --> 01:15:44.970
They're coming!

01:15:45.750 --> 01:15:46.230
Aristotle!

01:15:46.990 --> 01:15:49.170
The enemy of right on top of us!

01:15:50.060 --> 01:15:50.800
I'm sorry.

01:15:52.980 --> 01:15:53.780
It's dark.
